  "title": "How Financial Stress May Speed Up Brain Aging and Increase Dementia Risk",
  "summary": "Financial stress has long been associated with poor mental and physical health, but growing evidence suggests it may also affect brain health over time. Recent research indicates that people who experience long-term financial hardship may face a greater risk of faster brain aging, cognitive decline, and potentially Alzheimer's disease. While occasional money worries are common, persistent financial struggles appear to have a much deeper impact. Researchers say that chronic economic hardship can",
